# Security Rules

- Never log passwords, OTPs, tokens, card data or sensitive personal data.
- Hash passwords and OTPs appropriately.
- Enforce rate limits/brute-force controls where required.
- Rotate/revoke refresh tokens according to the authentication design.
- Reject customer tokens on admin APIs.
- Enforce role/permission checks server-side.
- Validate ownership for customer resources.
- Verify payment signatures/authenticity and prevent replay.
- Use idempotency for retry-sensitive financial/state-changing operations.
- Never store raw card information.
- Protect audit logs from unauthorized modification/access.
- Security fixes must not be weakened to satisfy UI behavior.
